WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:04.773
Emily Blunt is starring in one of the&nbsp;
summer's biggest movies — and after that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.773 --> 00:00:07.173
she's taking a break for a while. Here's why.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:12.060
The British actress revealed, in conversation&nbsp;
with Bruce Bozzi on his podcast "Table for Two,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.300
that she's set to take some time away&nbsp;
from acting now that her latest movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.320
"Oppenheimer," is set to release soon.&nbsp;
Blunt appears in Christopher Nolan's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.700
latest epic as Katherine Oppenheimer, wife&nbsp;
to Cillian Murphy's J. Robert Oppenheimer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.100
and apparently, that'll be her&nbsp;
last role for the next year.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.480
Blunt has two daughters — 7-year-old&nbsp;
Violet and 9-year-old Hazel — with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.400
husband John Krasinski, and as she told Bozzi,&nbsp;
she wants to enjoy their childhood more fully.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.720
"This year, I'm not working. I worked quite&nbsp;
a bit last year and my oldest baby is nine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.320
so we're in the last year of single&nbsp;
digits. And I just feel [like] there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.135
are cornerstones to their day that&nbsp;
are so important when they're little.

00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:47.679
She continued,

00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:51.180
"And it's, 'Will you wake me up?&nbsp;
Will you take me to school? Will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.680
you pick me up? Will you put me to&nbsp;
bed?' And I just need to be there."

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.000
Ultimately, Blunt said she feels guilty about&nbsp;
potentially missing her daughters' childhoods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.425
and she thinks that's common for&nbsp;
moms. She added on the podcast,

00:01:03.425 --> 00:01:09.480
"I think maybe all mothers are. You're&nbsp;
just prone to feeling bad for, God forbid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.870
wanting something outside of being a mother."

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.520
Blunt was clear about wanting&nbsp;
to take time away from acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.580
so she could spend more time with her&nbsp;
daughters — and it definitely doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.960
seem like she wants them to follow her&nbsp;
lead and become actors themselves. In a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.280
June interview with Harper's Bazaar UK ahead of&nbsp;
the release of "Oppenheimer," Blunt revealed,

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.960
"My toes curl when people tell me, 'My daughter&nbsp;
wants to be an actress.' I want to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.760
'don't do it!' Because it's a hard industry and&nbsp;
it can be very disappointing. A lot of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.720
tell you not to take things personally –&nbsp;
but it's completely personal, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.401
when you're being judged on how you look. So&nbsp;
you just have to endure that side of things."

00:01:44.401 --> 00:01:48.180
It's clear that Blunt, like many women in&nbsp;
the public eye trying to balance successful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.020
careers and parenthood, is frustrated by&nbsp;
the notion that you can't "have it all."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.260
Even though she's unequivocal&nbsp;
about this break from acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.040
she's also as ambitious as ever.&nbsp;
Acknowledging to Harper's Bazaar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.820
that she's pleased that equal pay has become&nbsp;
a bigger discussion in Hollywood, Blunt said,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.960
"Ambition is healthy – it shouldn't be seen&nbsp;
as a negative thing. It's about knowing your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.297
worth and what you bring to a project,&nbsp;
and never apologizing for doing well."

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.940
When all is said and done, it seems fair to&nbsp;
say that Blunt deserves a break considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:19.500
just how many projects she's filmed lately. She&nbsp;
stars in the Amazon miniseries "The English,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.600
and beyond "Oppenheimer," Blunt has several&nbsp;
major movies already banked; later in 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.800
her film "Pain Hustlers," which tells the dark&nbsp;
story of the modern pharmaceutical industry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.520
arrives in theaters. Her action&nbsp;
thriller alongside Ryan Gosling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.500
David Leitch's "The Fall Guy," is set to release&nbsp;
in 2024, with Blunt playing the ex-girlfriend to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.300
Gosling's stuntman who's trying to direct her own&nbsp;
film within the film. She's also reuniting with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:47.400
Krasinski for the ensemble comedy "IF," which is&nbsp;
slated for a spring 2024 release and features a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:52.380
packed cast including Fiona Shaw, Bobby Moynihan,&nbsp;
Steve Carell, Phoebe Waller-Bridge, and more.

00:02:52.894 --> 00:02:56.520
Speaking of Krasinski, there are always&nbsp;
whisperings about a third "Quiet Place"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.620
movie — and Blunt has starred in both of the&nbsp;
films. A spin-off prequel starring Lupita Nyong'o,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:06.000
"A Quiet Place: Day One," is on the way,&nbsp;
but as far as the mainline franchise goes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.500
nothing's been announced yet. For now, though,&nbsp;
Blunt has more than earned her time away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.813
acting — though audiences will undoubtedly&nbsp;
be happy whenever she chooses to return.

